{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1437941-help-with-treasure-creation-plz","id":1437941,"title":"Help with treasure creation plz?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-04T04:55:34-08:00","id":1437941,"title":"Help with treasure creation plz?","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> Have been going over the treasure creation and use section on the C20 and while there are some rules, it seems many parts of treasure creation are still narrative. I wanted to run by some treasures I thought up and ask your opinions. So look on these below and write what you think!<ul><li>Everliving Mask 5: A mask imbued by lvl5 of Pyretics - Phoenix Song. This one is pretty straightforward, if one waring the mask dies - their body burns up, while lava bubbles out of the mask and forms the new body. each activation a point of glamour is consumed. Just think this is pretty thematic.</li> <li>Biting Blade 1: Pretty Basic one, a blade imbued with lvl 1 of Dragons Ire. The problem here is I can't decide what bonus would it give. A specialized character could easily get like 6-7 successes on DI. Would assigning that much bonus to the weapon be reasonable? A large blade with already 4 damage + 7 would get to 11 damage. Alternatively, how would I arrange it's activation? like, roll attack and then... roll attack again, but add previous successes? Also, would it be necessary to spend glamour for that? I mean, you are already using a roll to activate/use the item and it doesn't do anything explicitly magical so... Also, would it be possible to give it Aggravated damage? Maybe make it a lvl 2 treasure or hunt down a chimera with aggro damage for materials?</li> <li>Belt of Strength 1: Using same Art as above and with pretty much the same questions. Would adding the same strength bonus of +7 be appropriate? should it be activated by glamour? I think it should, as belt doesn't really DO the action itself, unlike a blade. and how long would the bonus last in that case?</li> <li>Extra Health 3: something using Primal 3 to grant extra HP. How much HP would be appropriate? Again, getting a full HP stack with specialized character is quite possible. But what about a treasure? What about activation?</li> <li>Holly Cloak 4: Using Lvl4 Summer - Faerie Ring we enchant a cloak to hide anyone wearing it and curse anyone that dares to attack the one wearing it. Now, how many protection/stealth dice? Taking into account average of 4 dice pool for humans, would the changeling wearing it be practically invisible for mundanes? How many successes would be appropriate?</li> </ul>oh, and what about using chronos 5 to stop time. e.i accelerate it for user? description says you use it to basically age things. which is silly, cuz Autumn already does that. So I thought, if you use it on the user itself to give days worth of time in a few seconds. So subjectively for the user time would just stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 03-05-2021, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}